course: dictionary
lesson: 3004
title: Dusk, the time between day and night
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Dusk is the time in the evening just after the sun has set. It is getting dark, but it is not fully dark yet. You can often work out a word like dusk from the words around it. «At dusk the Rat dresses everybody for the expedition» tells you it is an evening time, when people get ready to go out.
explain: Look at the clues in another sentence. «Bracken Cave in Texas has millions of bats that fly out at dusk to eat insects.» Bats fly out when the light is fading, so dusk must be the time when it starts to get dark. Try your meaning in the sentence: "fly out when it is getting dark" makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Dusk has a partner word: dawn, the time in the morning when the sun comes up. Dawn starts the day and dusk ends it. The phrase «from dawn to dusk» means the whole time there is daylight, from the first light to the last.
fact: Dusk is the time just after sunset, when it is getting dark but not fully dark.
fact: Dusk also means the dim light at that time.
fact: Dawn is the matching time in the morning, when the sun is coming up.
fact: «Dusk falls» means it is starting to get dark.
fact: Many animals, such as bats, foxes, deer and rabbits, are most active at dusk and dawn; these animals are called crepuscular.
exercise: «The children had to be home by dusk.» What is dusk? | Midnight, when it is fully dark | A cold, windy afternoon | The morning, when the sun comes up | *The time just after sunset, when it is getting dark
exercise: Which word means the opposite of dusk, the time when the sun comes up? | *Dawn | Sunset | Noon | Midnight
exercise: «Starlings swirl over the roofs at dusk.» Find and copy one word that names the time when it starts to get dark. | *dusk | swirl | roofs | starlings
test: Why do drivers find dusk hard? | Because the roads are closed | *Because it is hard to see clearly, so bright or reflective clothes help | Because cars go faster at dusk | Because the sun is too bright
test: «Foxes and rabbits are most active from dusk to dawn.» What does dawn mean here? | The middle of the night | The time when the sun goes down | *The time in the morning when the sun comes up | The time in the afternoon when school ends
exam: «Lions hunt mostly from dusk to dawn.» Which word means about the same as dusk? | Midday | Noon | Dawn | *Twilight
